Working with others
This competency is about working cooperatively in a range of contexts for many different 
purposes. When structured well, working with others can enrich students’ learning and deepen 
their understanding of the dynamics of pairs, groups, and teams. Students can further develop 
their social and emotional skills and their understanding and appreciation of the talents, opinions, 
experiences and personalities of their peers, teachers and others. Working with others can 
deepen students’ appreciation of the importance of diversity and inclusion. It gives students 
opportunities to get better at navigating emotions, challenges, and conflicts which may arise, and 
to figure out how to negotiate a way forward. Technology is an increasingly important tool which 
can both support and present challenges to working with others.

